<title>FRANCE: French Dec trade surplus 11.33 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French Dec trade surplus 11.33 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus in December of 11.328 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in November of 8.867 billion, provisional customs office data showed.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in November of 9.50 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					   Dec	Nov</p>
<p> Trade balance		     11.328    8.867</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)    14.341    8.101</p>
<p> Imports			    118.044  113.096</p>
<p> Exports			    129.372  121.963</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	    5.797    4.617</p>
<p> Energy balance		    -7.780   -8.452</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance    9.170    8.766</p>
<p> Airbus exports	  5.008 (11 planes) 2.886 (6)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		    2.896    0.247</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports	     130.002  121.094</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports	     115.661  112.993</p>
<p> European Union		     3.454    3.523</p>
<p> Germany				1.047    0.187</p>
<p> Japan				 -1.869   -1.298</p>
<p> United States		     -2.291   -2.576</p>
<p>Cumulative 12-month figure for 1996:</p>
<p> Unadjusted balance	     122.340   97.803</p>
</text>
